  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the following ion/compounds</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e8fb8e10-64c2-4b24-9dd2-ad638a9edc89-image.png\" style=\"width: 243px; height: 228px;\" /></p><p>The main difference between aromatic antiaromatic and nonaromatic is that aromatic means having a delocalized pi electron system with (4n +2) electrons and antiaromatic means having a delocalized pi electron system with 4 electrons whereas nonaromatic means there is no delocalized electron system in that molecule.</p>",
